From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: no_trace <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 11:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ghosthook: clear pending EL0 SS at bounded trace stop

A bounded trace consumes its final HWSS exception before Linux reaches
single_step_handler().  user_disable_single_step() clears TIF_SINGLESTEP but
intentionally does not change the current exception frame's SPSR.SS bit.
Returning to EL0 with that pending bit set produces one unowned HWSS event,
which falls through to the stock handler and delivers SIGTRAP to the target.

Clear SPSR.SS in the consumed final exception frame after relinquishing
TIF_SINGLESTEP.  Active (non-final) events retain the prior rewind behavior.

---
 arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c
@@ -138,8 +138,13 @@
 	gh_ss_trace_record_locked(regs);
 	gh_ss_trace.hits++;
 	if (gh_ss_trace.hits >= gh_ss_trace.limit) {
-		/* The bounded session owns this SS request and may clear it. */
+		/*
+		 * user_disable_single_step() clears TIF_SINGLESTEP only.  Clear
+		 * the pending SPSR.SS bit in this exception frame as well, or the
+		 * EL0 return takes one unowned HWSS trap and receives SIGTRAP.
+		 */
 		user_disable_single_step(current);
+		user_fastforward_single_step(current);
 		gh_ss_trace.ss_owned = false;
 		gh_ss_trace.active = false;
 	} else {
-- 
